/* ---- fireworks from the cruise ships (OPEN WORLD, user Oct 27) ----
   "All the cruise ships have a button for fireworks. You see the little trail go up and then it explodes into these nice
   firework shapes." One rocket a press ("it will be more fun"), no reload at all (user Oct 27, 14:56: "Titanic should have
   fireworks. And it should not have a 'recharge' time, it defeats the purpose, you can do many as often as you want") -
   the cruise ships and the liner (FW_SHIPS); only so many in the air at once, the oldest let go to make room. Every press is
   different - another colour, another shape, another way (straight up, or leaning one way or the other) - and it always
   bursts above and around her, never far off. The sequence (user Oct 27: "We should see the little rocket shoot out and
   then do this firework explosion, and the little trails falling down"): the little rocket shoots up from her deck with a
   thin sparkling trail; it bursts; the streaks and twinkles fade and drop as little trails falling down; a little smoke
   is left at the centre, fading (the game's smoke, spawnSmoke). A bang a moment later, as from far off.
   The look is the user's picture (gen/open/ref/fireworks_ref_oct27.png), in the game's pixels: crisp stepped lines a
   pixel or two wide with bright tips -
   - the chrysanthemum: a full ball of straight streaks, all about the same length, lighter at their tips, round a dark
     point, and inside it a smaller burst of short, slightly curved strokes in a second colour (pink, pale yellow-green);
   - the willow: sparser streaks with a bright dash at each end, the lower ones longer, drooping as falling trails, fainter
     thin trails between (blue-violet and lavender);
   - the glitter: a wide round cloud of four-pointed twinkles of different sizes, faint thin dark lines back to the centre
     (white and cream);
   - and the others: the peony (a round ball of stars), the ring, the crackle (its stars popping into white flashes).
   Fading, a burst keeps fewer, smaller stars, its streaks going blue-grey, the smoke left behind.
   At night they glow, lighting the water and the ship under them a little (drawn after the night's tint, lateLit); by
   day they still go off, paler. They hurt nothing (no hits at all); birds near a burst fly off. A sinking cruise ship
   can't fire. The player's button (the action slot: X, a pad's third button); the CPU's cruise ships let a few off now and
   then after dark by themselves. */
const FW_SHIPS = new Set(['cruise', 'liner']);      // (the ships with the FIREWORKS button: the liner too, user Oct 27 14:56)
const FW_MAX = 24, FW_BITS_MAX = 1400;               // (at most this many rockets and bursts at once - the oldest goes; never a press refused)
const FW_CPU_GAP = 1;                                // (a CPU's salvo: about a second between rockets)
const fireworks = [];                                // (the rockets and bursts)
// (Nov 1) the little sparks and embers falling: a column table, a row a bit in the order made - fwBitRow (a rocket's trail, a
