// (user Nov 2, 12:24: "Motor boat, when spawned in the editor, its blank") a boat is drawn in the pass of the water it is on
// - a lake's (the land's pass) or the sea's - never by its kind: a motor boat was always a lake boat, so one at sea was drawn
// only behind the sea's water. One rule for every boat and yacht, everywhere a lake and the sea differ - which pass draws it,
// its shadow, depth charges, the night's anchoring, how far it may be driven: the water under it (onLakeW, waterSpanAt).
// b.lake / j.lake only says the lakes' builder made it ([lo, hi] of its lake: made again when the land is rebuilt)
const onLakeW = x => inCountry(x);                              // (OPEN WORLD and its ground not sea; the sea duel: all sea)
// the stretch of the water at x a boat may use, m in from its shores - read from the water itself, round where the boat is
// (user Nov 2 14:22, a motor boat in the editor's PLAY "all I can do is turn it": the old answer - its LAND tab lake's, else its
// SEAS row's - knew nothing of the water the terrain shapes make (a pocket with its own level, LAKE LEVELS 632): a boat on such
// water was given the nearest sea's span and snapped to its end every step). One rule for every water - sea, lake, pocket: wet
// where the ground is under the water's surface (not land, or land the water stands over), out to WSPAN_R each side - the boat
